  "title": "Taking an Uber in Nairobi — Part 2",
  "category": "transport",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "order": 2,
  "culturalNote": "Nairobi drivers love a chat. Once the destination is sorted, expect small talk: your name, where you're from, what you do. Answering in Swahili — even a few words — goes a long way. The ride ends the way most do: agree the price, say kwa heri. You're the mteja again; this time the conversation goes further.",
  "startingPoint": "Picking up where Part 1 left off — the driver asks which side of Westlands you want.",
